    {
      "id": "cor-the-center-is-a-polynomial-algebra-of-rank-many-generators",
      "status": "published",
      "depth": 3,
      "path": [
        "cor-every-system-of-parameters-is-regular-in-a-cohen-macaulay-module",
        "lem-reflection-basic-invariants-form-a-regular-sequence",
        "thm-chevalley-shephard-todd-for-finite-weyl-groups",
        "cor-the-center-is-a-polynomial-algebra-of-rank-many-generators"
      ],
      "direct_branches": [
        "lem-reflection-basic-invariants-form-a-regular-sequence"
      ],
      "all_reachable_incoming_uses": [
        {
          "supplier": "thm-chevalley-shephard-todd-for-finite-weyl-groups",
          "fields": [
            "deps"
          ],
          "body_paragraphs": [
            "2.1 The Weyl group is a finite real reflection group on the rank-$r$ space $\\mathfrak h^*$, so [[thm-chevalley-shephard-todd-for-finite-weyl-groups]] gives $S(\\mathfrak h)^W\\cong \\mathbb C[f_1,\\dots,f_r]$ for homogeneous algebraically independent generators. Thus step 1.1 already proves the polynomial-algebra assertion. [step 1.1]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "claim_sha256": "ee3890e97a8a52302a1cc04819b17f52ad5f6b84048e9ad80a9152a3d9b061f5",
      "disposition": "repaired_explicit_AC_by_shard07",
      "current_reachable": true,
      "current_claim_sha256": "ee3890e97a8a52302a1cc04819b17f52ad5f6b84048e9ad80a9152a3d9b061f5",
      "current_all_reachable_incoming_uses": [
        {
          "supplier": "thm-chevalley-shephard-todd-for-finite-weyl-groups",
          "fields": [
            "deps"
          ],
          "body_paragraphs": [
            "2.1 By [[def-root-reflections-and-the-weyl-group-action]], the Weyl group is generated by the root reflections. They act on the positive-definite real span of the roots and permute its finite spanning root set, so $W$ is a finite real reflection group on that rank-$r$ real space. Its complexification is $\\mathfrak h^*$. Under Choice, [[thm-chevalley-shephard-todd-for-finite-weyl-groups]] gives $S(\\mathfrak h)^W\\cong \\mathbb C[f_1,\\dots,f_r]$ for homogeneous algebraically independent generators. Thus step 1.1 already proves the polynomial-algebra assertion. [step 1.1, given]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
